# Monitoring & Metrics

> Analyzed from commit: `baf9c7bcc307ed9358ad59886a5536366a050012` on 2026-09-17
> Source paths: `pkg/monitoring/`, `pkg/metrics/`

## Package Purpose

Forklift exposes `mtv_*` Prometheus metrics for migration/plan lifecycle observability
and vSphere XCOPY copy-offload performance. Metric definitions and recording loops live
in `pkg/monitoring/metrics/forklift-controller/`. The HTTP serving layer is split between
the controller binary (`cmd/forklift-controller/main.go`) and a reusable TLS helper
(`pkg/metrics/promethousutil.go`) used by volume populators.

---

## Prometheus Endpoint

### forklift-controller (production path)

```
cmd/forklift-controller/main.go
  ├── promhttp.Handler() on :2112/metrics  (plain HTTP, default registry)
  └── controller-runtime --metrics-bind-address=127.0.0.1:8080/metrics

operator/config/default/manager_auth_proxy_patch.yaml
  └── kube-rbac-proxy :8443 → upstream :8080  (TLS + RBAC for Prometheus)

operator/config/prometheus/monitor.yaml
  └── ServiceMonitor scrapes :8443/metrics (scheme: https)
```

All `promauto`-registered metrics appear on both `:2112` and `:8080` because they share
the default Prometheus registry.

### Volume populators (sidecar jobs)

`pkg/metrics/promethousutil.go` → `StartPrometheusEndpoint(certsDirectory)`:

- Generates self-signed TLS cert/key at startup
- Serves `/metrics` over HTTPS on port **8443**
- Used by `cmd/ovirt-populator/` and `cmd/openstack-populator/`

> Note: upstream filename is `promethousutil.go` (typo preserved).

